    "_info": {
      "id": "isthmus_boundary_7623_floor_raises_gasused",
      "comment": "Same 1000-byte all-nonzero calldata as isthmus_boundary_gaslimit_below_floor, but gasLimit=100000 (comfortably above both the normal-intrinsic 37000 and the floor 61000), so the tx succeeds -- but op-geth's own reported gasUsed must be the *floor-adjusted* 61000, not the lower 37000 a naive normal-intrinsic-only computation would produce (EIP-7623's floor REPLACES the reported gas when it exceeds normal usage, per state_transition.go's `if st.gasUsed() \u003c floorDataGas { st.gasRemaining = st.initialGas - floorDataGas }`). This is the *normal-tx* counterpart of FINDING-1 (which is scoped to deposit txs only) -- a genuinely new differential surface for this wave.",
